#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166452 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dddc6159-ac4a-50ac-a366-08a4b809c925" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Particular Solution of an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/id #uuid "c5e60742-2571-5100-96be-a7578e6dda07" :question/math-academy-id "e-21540" :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/assets/eaf224db946e02695b83465fa548948a27e7587c7d4b270c604c897cdd4a2228.png)\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/assets/b7ae867ae694152125bc8cdf1ee7ab34c52b0c050408db3d2da86c7cbbc88493.png)\nFind the general solution of the system." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\mathbf{x}_c(t) + \\mathbf{x}_p(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{x}_c(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/assets/c68bfa253f23fb2c116b8769744e6fd22b7b898047e3ef3fe97f66dd91fefaa1.png)\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is exponential. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also exponential, i.e.\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/assets/b270d56283fdced6971e1a00fc3e642e379fc9348a0e4fb17a97ba6db2d8fc13.png)\nwhere $a,b$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of $\\mathbf{x}_p$ with respect to $t$ gives\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/assets/ca497159ae72a8b87997c78815119bb3de53782878cb2209072dcc505c902f37.png)\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute $\\mathbf{x}_p$ and $\\mathbf{x}'_p$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{e}^{7t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{7t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{7t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 7[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}7a \\\\ 7b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3a+b \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}7a \\\\ 7b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3a+b-1 \\\\ b-3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3a+b-1=7a \\\\ b-3=7b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get \n\n$$\nb - 7b = 3\n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\nb = -\\dfrac12.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n3a - \\dfrac12 - 1 = 7a\n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\na = -\\dfrac38.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/assets/fff596d40155dc7787910405557a722b5258890e3fae88f60842de92fac47177.png)\n\nAnd thus, the general solution is given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/assets/dc74c06c84905f8490932369e24cecd8f3b7eb64fdc4413e42c2f8bc1a3f3cbd.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166453 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d5ab3ac-770b-58c9-b30f-659773ea1a20" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem for an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/id #uuid "6f03c3e2-26dc-5ef3-90d9-9b80feac1ad4" :question/math-academy-id "e-21541" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/assets/5b0bb8069abe99949fc52c0be82c22f5879d7ca0ac334af396f47efa41ae0b5e.png)\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/assets/f220005265275c9297b7beef58777203a94351cb4957a26ca630802664759dc5.png)" :question/worked-solution "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/assets/40f93d12ebe4519dc4aa15f0df4b568ffa25f25afd99ec45130b569083c21fe0.png)\nwhere $c_1,c_2$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of $c_1$ and $c_2.$ Substituting $t = 0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{0} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot {e}^{0} \\\\ {e}^{0}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}-0+4 \\\\ -{0}^{2}+2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+4 \\\\ {c}_{2}+2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+4=6 \\\\ {c}_{2}+2=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $c_1 = 2.$ From the second equation, we have $c_2 = -1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/assets/948088eb5d495f3d8a8a96f038b5b036b53fa398544f9faedbb08026e96b661e.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166454 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eecbfc4-f7eb-5d4c-bea6-8fd21839804c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Form of a Particular Solution for Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/id #uuid "a5c44ae4-e55b-512f-ac1c-46f62950c1f4" :question/math-academy-id "e-21543" :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/assets/c9810bd07c9da4bd3d803740a85ce484cd92f4a0d8cb73af75d53602f8611a72.png)\nA complementary solution to this system is given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/assets/85139452af923a4f7b793fc47454cb99579ce0fa68ae33de3a15747501f624ef.png)\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as $\\mathbf{x}(t)=\\mathbf{x}_c(t)+\\mathbf{x}_p(t),$ where $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution $\\mathbf{x}_p(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t)=\\mathbf{x}_c(t)+\\mathbf{x}_p(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{x}_c(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/assets/13785393b66b769c10efcbf7cf9f1bb4f05c412a1ddb8649427b659728c7bd3e.png)\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is sinusoidal. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also sinusoidal, i.e.\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/assets/4b2dbbf0847dc9ea9f438e3848dca79da5f4e3f4473ab325a5f2c48e8b77e98c.png)\nwhere $a_1,a_2,b_1,b_2$ are constants that are to be determined."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166455 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51834713-edc2-5af3-a0dc-fb54ea4040c6" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs in Matrix Form"}] :question/id #uuid "aabc0f35-fdfc-573a-8d86-ada823a380a4" :question/math-academy-id "e-21544" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)+4{t}^{2}+t-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-{t}^{2}+5t+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite the system of linear ODEs in matrix form." :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite our system, highlighting the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=(-2)\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+(-1)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+4\\cdot {t}^{2}+1\\cdot t+(-2) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+0\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+(-1)\\cdot {t}^{2}+5\\cdot t+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in matrix form:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/assets/1247ff4c5147a3d08c411ac0ecdfd6ef56a0683797cfa5a39856a840c129a250.png)\nwhere ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068256/assets/da94081e0c87897fa4daece41902fb1ae6774725559c687189a9de66160571a4.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51834713-edc2-5af3-a0dc-fb54ea4040c6" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs in Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6853ddeb-9eb4-53e8-8c13-0658af5f1aa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6853ddeb-9eb4-53e8-8c13-0658af5f1aa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357028} :answer-field/id #uuid "a603db14-0f66-5114-b73d-4a81108e559c" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164033} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0746b256-a32d-581c-bbbd-d35ebe6395da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0746b256-a32d-581c-bbbd-d35ebe6395da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357024} :answer-field/id #uuid "c04fef2b-e214-5405-b695-49022bf6c23c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164034} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9bc97a0-ecbf-581c-b33b-55238f84c2ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9bc97a0-ecbf-581c-b33b-55238f84c2ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357023} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0d55fdb-0228-5247-8794-4dd7226c75a9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164035} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4dcb3ae-d430-572a-bcf2-e6339750931f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4dcb3ae-d430-572a-bcf2-e6339750931f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357027} :answer-field/id #uuid "daa851e2-39ab-5170-80c7-31369e65152d" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164036} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49354103-6ce3-5201-a04b-19f88ab8833b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49354103-6ce3-5201-a04b-19f88ab8833b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357029} :answer-field/id #uuid "e96be42b-7f6b-54e8-a653-f6cbeb4ff961" :answer-field/key "field-7" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164037} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dcaa16f5-f401-5141-8ec3-98856631e796" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcaa16f5-f401-5141-8ec3-98856631e796" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357025} :answer-field/id #uuid "52218fc7-3c42-530b-8676-0fe430501706" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164038} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "949c5dac-4625-5e0e-96cb-aec9bbc6f9a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "949c5dac-4625-5e0e-96cb-aec9bbc6f9a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357026} :answer-field/id #uuid "54056f04-4689-59df-ba3e-649b6429f44a" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164039} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f03e6c41-051f-5401-836c-811baa5736dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f03e6c41-051f-5401-836c-811baa5736dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357030} :answer-field/id #uuid "70700e29-c77d-5aa8-a9d2-2a0e3cb8a9c7" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164040}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "90dda3ee-b3fe-59fe-9f9b-bbb2e1549a90" :question/math-academy-id "q-329268" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)+3t+2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)-t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe systems of linear ODEs above can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n| ${x}^{′}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,x(t)+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-3}} |  |  | $\\,\\,t+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |  |  | {{field-7}} |  |  | {{field-8}} |  |  |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite our system, highlighting the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=(-1)\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+3\\cdot t+2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+(-1)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+(-1)\\cdot t+0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in matrix form:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357031 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51834713-edc2-5af3-a0dc-fb54ea4040c6" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs in Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cb25a48-a5ca-5e07-be45-2b957dcfec8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357033} {:answer/id #uuid "23400029-b941-506a-87fd-483933c66cdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23400029-b941-506a-87fd-483933c66cdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357034} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0c27328-d693-57f1-8a8b-86cde188b47c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/i